8
00:00:15.924 --> 00:00:17.785
The LSTM, long short-term memory, from

9
00:00:17.785 --> 00:00:19.473
Hochreiter and Schmidhuber in nineteen

10
00:00:19.473 --> 00:00:21.464
ninety-seven, adds a second state, called

11
00:00:21.464 --> 00:00:21.551
c.

12
00:00:21.810 --> 00:00:23.455
Picture it as a conveyor belt running

13
00:00:23.455 --> 00:00:25.359
along the top of the layer, from one slot

14
00:00:25.359 --> 00:00:26.787
to the next: the cell state.

15
00:00:27.047 --> 00:00:28.735
At each slot the belt passes one point

16
00:00:28.735 --> 00:00:30.336
where every entry is multiplied by a

17
00:00:30.336 --> 00:00:32.414
number from zero to one: how much of it to

18
00:00:32.414 --> 00:00:32.630
keep.

19
00:00:32.890 --> 00:00:34.794
That number is the forget gate, which was

20
00:00:34.794 --> 00:00:35.833
added to the LSTM later.

21
00:00:36.093 --> 00:00:38.170
Then a point where something new is added:

22
00:00:38.170 --> 00:00:38.776
what to write.

23
00:00:39.036 --> 00:00:40.897
And the layer shows a squashed view of the

24
00:00:40.897 --> 00:00:42.931
belt as its hidden state, h, which goes on

25
00:00:42.931 --> 00:00:44.922
to layer two, the head, and back into the

26
00:00:44.922 --> 00:00:45.917
layer at the next slot.

27
00:00:46.353 --> 00:00:48.363
Nothing else touches the belt: one

28
00:00:48.363 --> 00:00:49.368
